Third-party component not covered by this License
-------------------------------------------------

The Samsung Health Sensor SDK (samsung-health-sensor-api-*.aar) is proprietary to Samsung Electronics
and is NOT part of this repository or of OpenTDI's published apps. Each user downloads it from Samsung under
Samsung's own license, which governs it, and adds it to their own devices (the phone app converts it and passes
it to the watch app). A developer may also place it in wear/libs/ for a local build (see wear/libs/README.md);
such builds are for that developer's own devices and must not be distributed.

The phone app includes sherpa-onnx (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx) and the ONNX Runtime it
bundles (MIT). The optional neural voice model is not in this repository or the app: tools/voice/fetch_voice_model.sh
downloads Kokoro-82M (Apache-2.0) with espeak-ng data (GPL-3.0).

To install the watch app from the phone, the phone app includes Kadb (Apache-2.0,
https://github.com/flyfishxu/Kadb), spake2-java (GPL-3.0, https://github.com/Flyfish233/spake2-java), Bouncy Castle
(MIT, https://www.bouncycastle.org) and Okio (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/square/okio). A phone app built with the
Samsung SDK in wear/libs/ also carries the watch app, and with it the SDK, so the rule above applies to it too.
To check a release: no class under com.samsung may be defined in either APK or in the phone's assets/watch.apk.
The phone app also includes D8 from R8 (BSD-3-Clause, https://r8.googlesource.com/r8), which converts the user's
own Samsung kit on the phone.

The :samsung-health-stub module is original OpenTDI code that mirrors the SDK's public API (as
documented in Samsung's public API reference) so the project compiles without the SDK; it contains
no Samsung code.


Not a medical device
--------------------

OpenTDI is wellness and research software. It is not a medical device and is not intended to
diagnose, treat, cure, mitigate or prevent any disease or condition. Data from the Samsung Health
Sensor SDK is for fitness and wellness information only.
